dschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"}}],"rulings":[{"oracle_id":"196962f0-6aff-4198-9e0c-eaf42aeaf147","published_at":"2022-09-09","source":"wotc","comment":"You may still activate any other equip or crew abilities that permanent has if you wish."},{"oracle_id":"196962f0-6aff-4198-9e0c-eaf42aeaf147","published_at":"2022-09-09","source":"wotc","comment":"Once either the equip {1} or crew 1 ability is activated, causing Astor, Bearer of Blades to leave the battlefield won't stop the ability from resolving."},{"oracle_id":"74a62c7b-4753-4af2-b7a1-9a4ae8988801","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc","comment":"Once the equip {0} ability is activated, causing Puresteel Paladin to leave the battlefield or causing its controller to control fewer than three artifacts won't stop the equip ability from resolving."},{"oracle_id":"74a62c7b-4753-4af2-b7a1-9a4ae8988801","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc","comment":"You may still activate the Equipment's other equip abilities if you wish."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"You may tap more creatures than necessary to activate a crew ability."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"When a Vehicle becomes a creature, that doesn’t count as having a creature enter the battlefield. The permanent was already on the battlefield; it only changed its types. Abilities that trigger whenever a creature enters the battlefield won’t trigger."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"Once a player announces that they are activating a crew ability, no player may take other actions until the ability has been paid for. Notably, players can’t try to stop the ability by changing a creature’s power or by removing or tapping a creature."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"Creatures that crew a Vehicle aren’t attached to it or related in any other way. Effects that affect the Vehicle, such as by destroying it or giving it a +1/+1 counter, don’t affect the creatures that crewed it."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"If a permanent becomes a copy of a Vehicle, the copy won’t be a creature, even if the Vehicle it’s copying has become an artifact creature."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"Once a Vehicle becomes a creature, it behaves exactly like any other artifact creature. It can’t attack unless you’ve controlled it continuously since your turn began, it can block if it’s untapped, it can be tapped to pay a Vehicle’s crew cost, and so on."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"Vehicle is an artifact type, not a creature type. A Vehicle that’s crewed won’t normally have any creature type."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"You may activate a crew ability of a Vehicle even if it’s already an artifact creature. Doing so has no effect on the Vehicle. It doesn’t change its power and toughness."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"For a Vehicle to be able to attack, it must be a creature as the declare attackers step begins, so the latest you can activate its crew ability to attack with it is during the beginning of combat step. For a Vehicle to be able to block, it must be a creature as the declare blockers step begins, so the latest you can activate its crew ability to block with it is during the declare attackers step. In either case, players may take actions after the crew ability resolves but before the Vehicle has been declared as an attacking or blocking creature."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"If an effect causes a Vehicle to become an artifact creature with a specified power and toughness, that effect overwrites the Vehicle’s printed power and toughness."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"Each Vehicle is printed with a power and toughness, but it’s not a creature. If it becomes a creature (most likely through its crew ability), it will have that power and toughness."},{"oracle_id":"bc822c9a-633f-4830-9cb3-9af6a80622e4","published_at":"2017-09-29","source":"wotc","comment":"Any untapped creature you control can be tapped to pay a crew cost, even one that just came under your control."},{"oracle_id":"ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc","comment":"If a creature enters the battlefield under your control and gains haste, but then loses it before attacking, it won't be able to attack that turn. This means that you can't use one Lightning Greaves to allow two new creatures to attack in the same turn."},{"oracle_id":"ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc","comment":"You can't simply unequip Equipment from a creature. If Lightning Greaves is attached to the only creature you control, you won't be able to attach other equipment to it (or target it with anything else) until you have another creature to which you can attach Lightning Greaves."},{"oracle_id":"9ebd9ceb-05a4-4387-b63e-4c62ead2b98b","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc","comment":"“Unattach Heartseeker” means just that — Heartseeker moves off the creature it was equipping and remains on the battlefield."},{"oracle_id":"9ebd9ceb-05a4-4387-b63e-4c62ead2b98b","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc","comment":"Heartseeker grants an ability to the equipped creature. The ability can target a creature with protection from artifacts (unless the equipped creature is an artifact creature)."},{"oracle_id":"9ebd9ceb-05a4-4387-b63e-4c62ead2b98b","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc","comment":"The equipped creature’s controller chooses whether or not to activate the activated ability. It doesn’t matter who controls Heartseeker."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed."},{"oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc","comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat."},{"oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc","comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes."},{"oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc","comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands."},{"oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc","comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks."},{"oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc","comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control."},{"oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc","comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it."},{"oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it."},{"oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it."},{"oracle_id":"8de50bda-1ef6-4ccf-9efc-fab10b7eb2e5","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"Fervent Champion's last ability reduces only the generic mana in equip abilities. If those costs are only {3}, {2}, or {1}, that equip ability will be free to activate if it targets Fervent Champion."}]}
